ersity (NIU), invites applications for instructor positions to create a pool for advance and short notice hiring. These will be part or full-time temporary instructor positions. Start dates vary based on programmatic needs.We are seeking potential candidates to offer high-quality te... View Details Bookmark Public Speaking Instructor, Communication (Creating a Pool for Anticipated Openings) FAC0397P Communication Faculty 09/30/2026 The Department of Communication invites applications for instructor positions to create a pool for advance- and short-notice hiring based on program need. These will be part-time or full-time temporary instructor positions. Start dates will be based on program needs. The Instructor is a temporary (non-tenure track) position with duties that include teaching the fundamentals of oral communicatio... View Details Bookmark Instructor, Biological Sciences (Creating a Pool for Anticipated Openings) FAC0393P Biological Sciences Faculty 09/30/2026 The Biological Sciences Instructor will be responsible for teaching various topics in Biology, including but not limited to, Introductory Biology, General Education, and Human Anatomical Sciences, at both the undergraduate level and graduate levels, supervising student teaching assistants, and holding office hours. Applicants may be required to provide “in person” instruction. View Details Bookmark English Instructor (Creating a Pool for Anticipated Openings) (21528) FAC0346P English Faculty 09/30/2026 The Instructor is a temporary (non-tenure track) position with duties that include teaching first-year composition and related courses. Possibility of teaching other courses as needed. View Details Bookmark Migrant Educator (36189) FAC0379P P-20 Center Faculty This position will be primarily focused on tasks which support and supplement educational needs of migratory farmworkers and their children. The skill most-valued in the Educator is in building trusting relationships with families that lead to tutoring, summer school, field trips and other family educational gatherings and more. The Educator must have reliable transportation (travel reimbursed)... View Details Bookmark Sales Instructor, Department of Marketing (Creating a Pool for Anticipated Openings) FAC0325P Marketing Faculty The part-time instructors in the sales area teach 3-6 credit hours per academic year. View Details Bookmark Global Marketing Instructor, Department of Marketing (Creating a Pool for Anticipated Openings) FAC0324P Marketing Faculty The part-time instructors in the global marketing area teach 3-6 credit hours per academic year. View Details Bookmark © 2019 Board of Trustees of Northern Illinois University All rights reserved. Back to Top Northern Illinois University 1425 W. Lincoln Hwy., DeKalb, IL 60115 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
