      "title": "Find your Career",
      "description": "Northern Illinois University | Search All Jobs Skip to Main Content Find your Career at Northern Illinois University! Toggle navigation Home Search All Jobs Log In /Create Account Help NIU Human Resources Search  Postings (30) Hide Search Options View all open Postings below, or enter search criteria to narrow your search. Keywords Posted Within Any time period Last Day Last Week Last Month Position Type No Selection Faculty Staff Extra Help Student Employees Graduate Assistant Post Doc View Results (30\n    ) Sort by Job Title Posting Number Department Postion Type Job Close Date Assistant Director of Adventures (4342) Specialty Factors Univ Recreation and Wellness Staff 09/18/2026 This position will provide leadership, direction, and oversight of a comprehensive Adventures program including special events, rentals, bouldering, and team-building. The person in this position plans, prepares and leads inclusive Adventure programming both on and off property. Programming includes, but is not limited to, kayaking, canoeing, biking, hiking, backpacking, rock climbing, special ... View Details Bookmark Program Assistant (3808) Architectural/Engineering Svcs Staff 09/10/2026 Under the supervision of the Director of Architectural and Engineering Services (AES), this position duties will include the following:Assist department staff with transition to TMA space management software for campus facilities floor plans integration and ongoing updates alligning with building modifications as they occur.Maintenance, organization and cataloguing of paper and digital drawings... View Details Bookmark Building Service Worker (3785) [MULTIPLE POSITIONS] Building Services Staff 09/14/2026 Under the direct supervision of a Building Service Foreman, the Builder Service Worker performs the necessary custodial work to meet and maintain Building Services’ high standards of cleanliness and sanitation. Perform other duties closely related to those defined in the class specifications. View Details Bookmark Director Campus Dining Retail (4634) Campus Dining Service Staff 09/17/2026 The Retail Dining Director position is critical to the successful operation, compliance, and continued growth of our retail dining program. This role provides leadership and oversight for over 25 full-time employees across seven locations, including branded locations, creating a level of operational complexity that requires dedicated management and accountability. The Retail Dining Director ens... View Details Bookmark Skill Advancement Coach - Child Welfare (4002) - Hiring Multiple Positions Psychology Staff Under the direction of the DCFS Director of the Office of Research and Child Well-Being, the Skill Advancement Coach provides structured, skill-based coaching to supervisors and other staff across DCFS/CWCA. This role strengthens supervisory capacity, improves team performance, and promotes alignment with DCFS values, well-being goals, and implementation science principles. The coach supports s... View Details Bookmark Education Advisor (4835) Decatur, IL - EXTENDED Ctr Child Welfare & Education Staff 09/09/2026 This position will be working out of Decatur-Springfield, IL.The Education Advisor provides problem resolution, subject matter expertise, advocacy, and guidance for educational wellbeing of children and youth in foster care (youth in care). The education advisor possesses extensive knowledge and skills that help youth navigate the complex network of education (general, special and post-secondar... View Details Bookmark Access Consultant (2810) [Multiple Positions] Disability Resource Center Staff 09/14/2026 The Access Consultant conducts the interactive process to determine reasonable accommodations for students with disabilities, resulting in students gaining access to curricular and co-curricular environments supported through legal mandates. Emphasis is on developing a deep relationship with students in an effort to better understand how the educational environment impacts access.Additionally, ... View Details Bookmark Student Conduct Coordinator (00002528) Student Conduct Staff 09/24/2026 Serving as the primary liaison between the Office of Student Conduct and Housing and Residential Life, the coordinator provides leadership in the administration of residential student conduct processes. This role is responsible for managing housing-related conduct cases and ensuring consistent, educational, and developmentally appropriate responses to student behavior within the residential com... View Details Bookmark Office Administrator (3471) [REPOST] STA3716P Psychology Staff 09/14/2026 The primary responsibility of this position is to provide leadership in carrying out all administrative functions of the Department of Psychology. The person in this position provides administrative supervision of the daily activities of the department and its staff.The person in this position has the complete confidence of the department chair; the work performed by this person is closely iden... View Details Bookmark Culinary Worker III – Cook (0544) [EXTENDED] [ MULTIPLE POSITIONS] Residential Dining Service Staff 09/10/2026 9-month position (Aug 16-May 15); actual start and end dates may vary based on academic calendar.This position is responsible for assisting with the assignment of work activities of kitchen helpers and student employees working in the food production area and is responsible for daily preparation of food items for Dining Services. Individual in this position works under the supervision of Food S... View Details Bookmark CPRG Clean Energy Programs Manager (36793) P-20 Center Staff 09/15/2026 The Clean Energy Program Manager oversees day-to-day operations of the Clean Building Navigator Grant Program and CEJA Capacity Grant Manager. This position ensures timely execution of tasks, coordination across staff and partners, delivery of high-quality outputs, and implementation of both programs. This role translates strategic direction into operational workflows and cross-community coordi... View Details Bookmark CPRG Statewide Energy Efficiency Navigator (36306) P-20 Center Staff 09/15/2026 The Statewide Energy Efficiency Navigator is responsible for supporting equitable access to energy efficiency and clean energy programs across Illinois, particularly in CEJA-designated communities and identified municipal utility and rural co-op communities not served during the initial phase of the Clean Building Navigator (CBN) program. This role maintains a comprehensive and up-to-date under... View Details Bookmark CPRG Ecosystem & Community Specialist (29294) P-20 Center Staff 09/15/2026 The Ecosystem & Community Specialist leads community engagement, technical assistance, and capacity development for Clean Building Navigator Program and CEJA Capacity Grant program grantees and community-based partners. This role ensures that community voice, equity, and organizational sustainability are embedded across program design and implementation.Who We Are SeekingBeyond experience a... View Details Bookmark IT Technical Associate (3797) University Libraries Staff 09/15/2026 Academic Affairs Technology Support (AATS) serves a critical role in supporting information technology across Academic Affairs. This position supports the University Libraries while also contributing to the broader Academic Affairs technology environment.The position provides technology support for library faculty, staff, and students; maintains endpoint devices, learning spaces, media systems,... View Details Bookmark Director of Information Security (4071) DoIT-Admin-Business-Finance Staff The Director of Information Security has direct management responsibility for the Information Security Office (ISO), Account Access, Business Continuity and IT Disaster Planning (BCDP) and IT physical security. Account Access, BCDP, ISO and IT Physical Security combine to represent a comprehensive umbrella of IT related security services and includes oversight and coordination of the NIU Inform... View Details Bookmark Program Advisor – University Honors Program (3012) University Honors Program Staff 09/10/2026 The Program Advisor (Engagement) is a student-centered support position that mentors and guides students in the University Honors Program through all aspects of program requirements, with a particular focus on co-curricular engagement, recruitment, and event-based outreach. This position plays a central role in daily contact with students through the implementation of advising and retention str... View Details Bookmark Dining Manager (3301) [REPOST] Residential Dining Service Staff 09/09/2026 Directs daily operations of one or more dining units to ensure employees have appropriate equipment, inventory, and resources to perform their jobs and meet goals and deadlines. Establishes operating standards and communicates to employees. Supervises daily activities and delegates duties. View Details Bookmark Cultural Resources Specialist (39214) VP Research and Innv Prtnrshp Staff This position supports IDOT’s cultural resource compliance program by reviewing Environmental Survey Requests (ESRs), archaeological eligibility assessments, and consultant-prepared reports to ensure compliance with Section 106 of the National Historic Preservation Act, Section 4(f), and relevant state laws. The Cultural Resources Specialist works within NIU’s Northern Illinois Center for Commu... View Details Bookmark Project Director for Tribal Partnerships (34825) VP Research and Innv Prtnrshp Staff NIU seeks a culturally informed and SOI-qualified professional to serve as a Tribal Relations Liaison within the university’s Northern Illinois Center for Community Sustainability (NICCS). This academic professional position is fully funded through a partnership with the Illinois Department of Transportation (IDOT) and supports respectful, legally compliant engagement between IDOT and Tribal Na... View Details Bookmark Senior Director of Gift Planning (34871) Gift Planning Staff The Impact You’ll MakeReporting to the Executive Director of Philanthropy and partnering closely with colleagues across the NIU Foundation and University, the Senior Director of Gift Planning serves as a key leader in advancing the institution’s philanthropic mission through strategic gift planning and donor engagement by:Providing strategic leadership for a comprehensive and collaborative gift... View Details Bookmark Northern Illinois Center for Community Sustainability (NICCS) Roadside Ecology Program Manager (3531) VP Research and Innv Prtnrshp Staff The Roadside Ecology Program Manager will serve as the main point-of-contact with the Illinois Department of Transportation and manage the workload of eleven Roadside Ecology staff to meet natural resource field survey and reporting needs for IDOT projects. The Program Manager will be principally responsible for reports from the program staff that outline regulatory documentation related to bio... View Details Bookmark Assistant Dean for the Part-Time J.D. Program and Lecturer (00005020) College of Law Staff This position is located at NIU Law’s new Naperville campus. This is an extraordinary opportunity for the right candidate to play a foundational role in growing a new legal program that will expand access to legal education for working professionals in the western suburbs of Chicago.The position has both administrative responsibilities and teaching responsibilities.Administrative Responsibiliti... View Details Bookmark Interdisciplinary Wildlife/Wetland Ecologist (35315) Multiple Positions VP Research and Innv Prtnrshp Staff Positions represent a balance of regulatory service work (approximately 60%) with applied research (approximately 40%). Interdisciplinary Ecologists will be assigned to either the Biological Team (focused on wildlife, threatened and endangered species, and multi-taxa surveys) or the Wetland Team (focused on wetland delineation, functional assessments, and aquatic resources). All positions requi... View Details Bookmark LGBTQI+ Diversity Trainer (4531) Psychology Staff Under the direction of DCFS the LGBTQI Diversity Trainer directs, coordinates, and manages statewide the Illinois Department of Children and Family (IDCFS) programs, initiatives, and training to ensure that appropriate services are provided to LGBTQI youth. View Details Bookmark Assistant Athletic Trainer (4866) Multiple positions STA3676P Intercollegiate Athletics Staff Responsible for assisting in the management and administration of all phases of the athletic training operations. View Details Bookmark Research Associate (39132) Education Systems Center Staff This position, located in Chicago, will be a hybrid between in-person and remote. The position will be focused on the tracking of business and policy implementation for early childhood funding equity. The position regularly exercises discretion and independent judgment involving complex tasks with appreciable latitude for unreviewed action or decision-making. View Details Bookmark Assistant Director of Alumni Engagement & Annual Giving (36475) Alumni Services Staff This role is integral to the success of alumni engagement and annual giving efforts, serving as a hub for coordination, execution, and continuous improvement across programs and initiatives.The Assistant Director leads and implements key components of alumni engagement and annual giving work, contributing to the development of new initiatives while ensuring existing programs run effectively. Th... View Details Bookmark Director of Learning Partnerships and Contracts (4241) College of Education Staff The Director of Partnerships and Contracts provides strategic leadership for developing, managing, and expanding contract-based educational programs and partnerships that advance the mission, impact, and financial sustainability of the College of Education. The Assoc. Director serves as the College’s primary liaison to external organizations and internal university partners, identifying and sec... View Details Bookmark Skills Lab Specialist (21123) Nursing Staff The Skills Lab Specialist supports the daily operations of the Nursing Skills Laboratory by providing coordination, instructional support, and operational oversight of skills-based learning activities. This role focuses on the preparation, facilitation, and evaluation support of student skills practice and testing, ensuring a consistent, organized, and high-quality learning environment. The Ski... View Details Bookmark Post Doctoral Fellow (36054) STA3341P Physics Staff Under the supervision of the NIU senior faculty and theory PIs of the project, the successful postdoctoral scholar will work on the theory and simulation of the dynamical processes in complex superconducting heterostructure relevant for superconducting digital logic devices. The obtained simulation results will be analyzed and verified with experimental observations in collaboration with the ex... View Details Bookmark © 2019 Board of Trustees of Northern Illinois University All rights reserved. Back to Top Northern Illinois University 1425 W. Lincoln Hwy., DeKalb, IL 60115 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
